## harness-engineering/guardrails.md

```markdown
# Harness Guardrails

The authoritative harness config is this plugin's docs-adjacent metadata file at `docs/harness-engineering/harness-engineering.json`.

`CLAUDE.md` is the repository-level rule map. `AGENTS.md -> CLAUDE.md` is required when `absence.agentContextAlias` is `required`; record no-overwrite conflicts in the updates log instead of claiming the alias is satisfied.

## Staged Gates

| Stage | Mode | Exit Gate |
| --- | --- | --- |
| 0 discovery | report | Inventory complete |
| 1 visibility | advisory | Config and docs validate |
| 2 local guardrails | warn | Local validator runs |
| 3 shared gates | error | CI or hook wrapper command passes and error findings fail |
| 4 ratchet | error new debt | Known violations trend down |

## Scoped Path Rules

| Path | Rule | Source |
| --- | --- | --- |
| src/domains/** | Follow configured layer model | ARCHITECTURE.md |
| docs/product-specs/**/*.md | User requirements name source, acceptance criteria, and validation surface | product specs and checks |

## Lifecycle

Every harness configuration, validation script, wrapper command, CI/hook template, and allowed command form is a lifecycle artifact that evolves with the project. Update the harness config, scripts, CI, and hooks together and keep them documented and validated as a unit.

Stages, hooks, required commands, and optional commands are declarative lifecycle gates. The config names each gate, enforcement mode, and command surface before CI or hooks enforce it.
```

